{
  "title": "Six-step local Craftax goal planning beyond no-op",
  "caption": "Six-step local goal planning with one frozen 512-dimensional JEPA checkpoint. Goals are generated by six random actions; execution uses fresh environment randomness independent of target generation, paired across policies. Goal success requires the exact target position after six actions and survival throughout warmup and execution. Left: all 384 starts from three 128-episode evaluation batches. Right: the 247 starts whose goal position differs from the initial position. Open loop plans once; receding-horizon control replans after each observation. Whiskers are 95% Wilson episode-level intervals for one trained model, not uncertainty over model training seeds. The exact native-color start and target images show evaluation seed 101, episode 5: the first stored scene with L1 goal displacement at least two, chosen without inspecting model outcomes. These results establish local goal-position control for this checkpoint, not general Craftax achievement or long-horizon reward competence.",
